ed a  spaceport  after going beyond earth it re-enters  the atmosphere and arrives at a floating  spaceport in another city  since starship is fully reusable the  price of a ticket will be drastically  reduced  but that doesn't mean it will be cheap  we don't yet know how much a trip will  cost but a cnbc reporter quoted spacex's  president and ceo  quinn shotwell singh at an event in 2019  that it will be cheaper than a first  class ticket  but a little more than economy shotwell  has also said previously that it would  be less than a business class fare  so it's still unclear what the price  will be but here's an example of  round-trip plan tickets from london's  heathrow airport  to new york's jfk about a month from now  an average economy ticket is around four  hundred dollars  for business class it's four thousand  and for first class about five thousand  besides the price there's another big  consideration spacex will need to  address  rockets are really noisy  that's the sound of one raptor engine  that powers starship  there are currently 31 of these planned  for the super heavy booster which lifts  starship into orbit  while another six are located on  starship itself  however musk has said starship could  actually make trips under 6 200 miles  without the need for the booster and  instead the spacecraft would fly with an  additional two to four engines  but because it would still have an  impact on residents the spaceport will  be located 20  miles offshore which means getting there  could take more time  than the actual flight as a comparison  the journey from new york's grand  central terminal to jfk  airport is about 14 miles musk has  suggested a hyperloop transit system  traveling hundreds of miles per hour  could ferry people to the spaceports  really quickly  and while spacex works at all its plans  the airline industry is also trying to  cut down on travel time supersonic  planes which travel faster than the  speed of sound could be returning  the 